# Keep-both union merge for the changelog: parallel PRs each append to
# [Unreleased], so a literal merge conflicts. The union driver keeps both sides.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# Same shape, same remedy (iss-118): DECISIONS.md is an append-only ledger of
# anonymous, dated, order-independent entries that never need identity, so two
# concurrent appends have nothing to actually disagree on. ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md
# left this list when its references section became a numbered, alphabetically
# ordered list: an insertion renumbers subsequent entries, so a union merge of
# two concurrent additions would silently interleave both sides' renumbered
# lines. A loud conflict is the correct outcome there.
.abcd/work/DECISIONS.md merge=union

# The committed git hooks are executed by bash on every platform that runs them,
# and a CRLF checkout makes the shebang line unparseable ("bad interpreter").
# Pinning LF keeps the guard runnable after a checkout with autocrlf on, and keeps
# the embedded scaffold template byte-identical to what it scaffolds.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
internal/core/ahoy/defaults/pre-commit text eol=lf
internal/core/ahoy/defaults/pre-merge-commit text eol=lf
# hooks/bootstrap.sh is executed by the harness on every SessionStart and is the
# one thing that provisions the plugin binary, so a CRLF checkout does not merely
# break a hook: it breaks the script that repairs the hooks.
hooks/*.sh text eol=lf
# The preflight and release gates invoke scripts/*.sh through their shebang (and
# via `bash scripts/...`); a CRLF checkout breaks both — a \r is a syntax error
# to bash — so the pinned pre-push hook would then die one hop later here.
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
# site-src/install.sh.tmpl is the committed source of the /install.sh the site
# serves: `abcd site build` copies its bytes out (plus one stamp comment) and
# users pipe the result straight into `sh`, where a trailing \r on every line
# is a syntax error — no shebang required to break it. A render from a CRLF
# checkout would publish an installer that cannot run.
site-src/install.sh.tmpl text eol=lf
